{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "RRTMLWHeating",
    "description": "Longwave heating of a model column from the RRTM up- and downwelling fluxes (WRF ra_lw_physics = 1, SUBROUTINE RTRN heating-rate loop 7000 and the TTEN/GLW/OLR mapping of SUBROUTINE RRTM in phys/module_ra_rrtm.F, WRF 4.8), written as the pressure-coordinate flux-divergence PDE  dT/dt = -(g/cp) dF_net/ds,  s = p_sfc - p  on the EarthSciDiscretizations grids/column_nonuniform_1d grid. The grid's interface coordinate `ze` is here the PRESSURE DISTANCE ABOVE THE SURFACE s = p_e[1] - p_e (Pa, monotone increasing with lev), so the grid's layer measure dz is the layer pressure thickness p_e[k] - p_e[k+1] and the imported face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces rule lowers D(F_net, lev) to (F_net[k+1] - F_net[k]) / (p_e[k] - p_e[k+1]); with the RRTM value of g/cp (HEATFAC) this is exactly RTRN's  HTR(L-1) = HEATFAC (FNET(L-1) - FNET(L)) / (PZ(L-1) - PZ(L)),  L = 1..NLAYERS, PZ in hPa, HTR in K/day, verified against the instrumented WRF dumps to real32 roundoff (this is the convention the instrumentation pass could not reproduce: HTR(L-1), not HTR(L), is the heating of layer L, and HTR(NLAYERS) is simply set to 0). Column mapping: RRTM indexes its column BOTTOM-UP like this grid -- RRTM layer L is model layer L for L <= NLEV (MM5ATM: PAVEL(L) = p(kte+1-L) undoes the top-down ordering of the RRTMLWRAD 1-D arrays), RRTM level L is the model interface L+1 (PZ(0) the surface p8w(1), PZ(NLEV) the model top p_top) -- and MM5ATM extends the column above p_top with NLAYERS - NLEV buffer layers of thickness deltap = 4 hPa down to PZ(NLAYERS) = 0 (temperatures from a standard profile offset to match the model top, constant water vapour 5e-6, model-top CH4/N2O, climatological ozone) so that the fluxes at the model interfaces include the emission of the atmosphere above the model top. Only the fluxes at the NLEV+1 MODEL interfaces enter this component (inputs F_up, F_dn of shape [lev_nodes], the first NLEV+1 entries of TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX); the buffer layers are heated by RTRN but their heating is discarded (RRTM: TTEN(K) = HTR(kte-K)/86400 for K = 1..kte, in the wrapper's top-down order). Outputs: dTdt (K/s, WRF TTEN reversed to bottom-up), dthdt = dTdt/exner (the increment RRTMLWRAD adds to RTHRATEN), glw = F_dn at the surface (GLW = TOTDFLUX(0)) and olr = F_up at the MODEL TOP (WRF sets OLR = TOTUFLUX(kte), the upward flux at p_top, not TOTUFLUX(NLAYERS) at the top of the RRTM column; the two differ by 3-7 W/m^2 in the reference run). The fluxes themselves (the RTRN two-stream sweep over 140 g-points and the gas optics) are the later stages of the RRTM transcription; this component is the flux-to-tendency stage that every longwave scheme shares. Inputs are REWRITE-TARGET ops `input_<name>` that the consumer lowers (in the inline tests through a per-test expression_template_imports library generated by tools/fill_tests.py, because esm-spec 6.6 parameter_overrides admit scalars only).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["radiation", "longwave", "rrtm", "heating-rate", "column", "wrf"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Mlawer, E. J., S. J. Taubman, P. D. Brown, M. J. Iacono, and S. A. Clough (1997). Radiative transfer for inhomogeneous atmospheres: RRTM, a validated correlated-k model for the longwave. J. Geophys. Res., 102(D14), 16663-16682.",
        "doi": "10.1029/97JD00237"
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF 4.8 phys/module_ra_rrtm.F: RTRN loop 7000 (lines 6655-6668, heating rate), RRTM lines 2341-2347 (TTEN/GLW/OLR), MM5ATM lines 4103-4150 (buffer layers above the model top), RRTMLWRAD lines 2029-2063 (column ordering)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "RRTMLWHeating": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": { "NLEV": "NLEV" }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../../../../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/face_flux_D_lev_supplied_faces.esm",
          "bindings": { "NLEV": "NLEV" }
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": { "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm" },
        "par": { "ref": "./rrtm_parameters.esm" }
      },
      "variables": {
        "F_up_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives `F_up` from the upstream component through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when the assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_F_up` to this parameter (see couplings/rrtm_lw_column.esm). Standalone, `input_F_up` is lowered to a dumped column by the test's library and this parameter is unused (default 0)."
        },
        "F_dn_in": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Coupling target (assembly input path): a shaped parameter that receives `F_dn` from the upstream component through a document-level `coupling.variable_map` (`param_to_var`) when the assembly's mount-edge template library lowers `input_F_dn` to this parameter (see couplings/rrtm_lw_column.esm). Standalone, `input_F_dn` is lowered to a dumped column by the test's library and this parameter is unused (default 0)."
        },
        "p_e": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": ["lev_nodes"],
          "description": "Interface (full-level) pressure, p_e[1] the surface pressure and p_e[NLEV+1] the model-top pressure p_top (WRF p8w, bottom-up; RRTM PZ(0..kte) times 100), consumer-supplied through `input_p_e`."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": ["lev_nodes"],
          "description": "The grid's interface coordinate: pressure distance above the surface s = p_e[1] - p_e, 0 at the surface and increasing upward, so that the column grid's finite-volume operators are taken with respect to pressure (the grid contract: a pressure- or mass-based column supplies its own monotone interface coordinate as ze)."
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Layer mid-point of the pressure coordinate, (ze[k] + ze[k+1])/2 (grid template column_cell_center)."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Layer pressure thickness p_e[k] - p_e[k+1] = ze[k+1] - ze[k] (grid template column_cell_thickness); the control measure read by the flux-divergence rule (RTRN: PZ(L-1) - PZ(L) in hPa)."
        },
        "F_up": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "shape": ["lev_nodes"],
          "description": "Upwelling longwave flux at the model interfaces (RRTM TOTUFLUX(0..kte), bottom-up), consumer-supplied through `input_F_up`."
        },
        "F_dn": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "shape": ["lev_nodes"],
          "description": "Downwelling longwave flux at the model interfaces (RRTM TOTDFLUX(0..kte), bottom-up), consumer-supplied through `input_F_dn`."
        },
        "F_net": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "shape": ["lev_nodes"],
          "description": "Net upward longwave flux F_up - F_dn at the model interfaces (RTRN FNET)."
        },
        "exner": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Exner function of the layer (WRF pi3d), consumer-supplied through `input_exner`; converts the temperature tendency into the potential-temperature tendency RTHRATEN."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Layer temperature (WRF t3d), the prognostic state, initialised from `input_T` and heated by dTdt."
        },
        "g_over_cp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K/m",
          "description": "RRTM's g/cp in SI, HEATFAC converted from K/day per (W/m^2/hPa) to K/s per (W/m^2/Pa): heatfac pa_per_hpa / seconds_per_day = 9.76748e-3 K/m (the dry-adiabatic lapse rate with RRTM's g and cp)."
        },
        "dTdt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K/s",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Longwave heating rate -(g/cp) dF_net/ds of each model layer (RRTM TTEN, reversed to bottom-up; HTR(L-1)/86400 for layer L)."
        },
        "dthdt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K/s",
          "shape": ["lev"],
          "description": "Potential-temperature tendency dTdt/exner (the increment RRTMLWRAD adds to RTHRATEN)."
        },
        "glw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "Downwelling longwave flux at the surface, F_dn[1] (RRTM GLW = TOTDFLUX(0))."
        },
        "olr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "WRF's OLR diagnostic: the upwelling longwave flux at the MODEL TOP, F_up[NLEV+1] (RRTM OLR = TOTUFLUX(kte)), which is not the flux at the top of the extended RRTM column (TOTUFLUX(NLAYERS), 3-7 W/m^2 lower in the reference run because the buffer layers above p_top absorb)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": "p_e", "rhs": { "op": "input_p_e", "args": [] } },
        {
          "lhs": "ze",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["kn"],
            "args": ["p_e"],
            "ranges": { "kn": { "from": "lev_nodes" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "-",
              "args": [
                { "op": "index", "args": ["p_e", 1] },
                { "op": "index", "args": ["p_e", "kn"] }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "zc",
          "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "column_cell_center", "bindings": { "ze": "ze" } }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dz",
          "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "column_cell_thickness", "bindings": { "ze": "ze" } }
        },
        { "lhs": "F_up", "rhs": { "op": "input_F_up", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "F_dn", "rhs": { "op": "input_F_dn", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": "F_net", "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["F_up", "F_dn"] } },
        { "lhs": "exner", "rhs": { "op": "input_exner", "args": [] } },
        { "lhs": { "op": "ic", "args": ["T"] }, "rhs": { "op": "input_T", "args": [] } },
        {
          "lhs": "g_over_cp",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": ["par.heatfac", "par.pa_per_hpa"] },
              "par.seconds_per_day"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dTdt",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              -1.0,
              "g_over_cp",
              { "op": "D", "args": ["F_net"], "wrt": "lev" }
            ]
          }
        },
        { "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["T"], "wrt": "t" }, "rhs": "dTdt" },
        { "lhs": "dthdt", "rhs": { "op": "/", "args": ["dTdt", "exner"] } },
        { "lhs": "glw", "rhs": { "op": "index", "args": ["F_dn", 1] } },
        {
          "lhs": "olr",
          "rhs": { "op": "index", "args": ["F_up", { "op": "+", "args": ["NLEV", 1] }] }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "scm_call1_evening_clear",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF@e42a269 (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver (rrtminit needs WRF's I/O layer for the k-distribution data), so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of tile column 1 (p8w, pi3d, t3d, bottom-up) and the RRTM fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX at the model interfaces (RRTM levels 0..kte, already bottom-up). Expected values: dTdt against HTR(0..kte-1)/86400 (the RTRN heating of RRTM layers 1..kte, i.e. HTR(L-1) is layer L), dthdt against the wrapper's RTHRATEN increment, F_net and dz against the identities on the inputs, glw = TOTDFLUX(0), olr = TOTUFLUX(kte). Measured mismatch of this component against HTR over the four regimes is <= 2.4e-10 K/s in Linf (5e-6 of the column maximum of |dTdt|) and <= 5.3e-6 relative at the three largest-|dTdt| layers (real32 arithmetic of HEATFAC*(FNET(L-1)-FNET(L))/(PZ(L-1)-PZ(L)): differences of O(300 W/m^2) fluxes and O(1000 hPa) pressures carried in single precision), so the column assertions use Linf_error abs 1e-9 K/s (about 1e-5 of the column maximum) and the spot checks rel 1e-5, the real32 contract; the identities (F_net, dz, glw, olr, g_over_cp) use rel/abs 1e-9. The scheme is diagnostic (no time step), so no small-dt replay is involved. Regime: first radiation call (call 1, 19:00 UTC = 12:34 LST), clear sky (cldfra = 0, no condensate), tsk = 288.0 K, glw = 258.1 W/m^2, olr (model top) = 251.5 W/m^2; strongest cooling in the lowest layer and at layers 38-39 (the moist layer top).",
          "parameter_overrides": {},
          "expression_template_imports": [
            {
              "ref": "./tests/scm_call1_evening_clear_inputs.esm"
            }
          ],
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-09
          },
